{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-03 decision approved: maximum 3 physical wire/subprocess invocations across one atomic logical desired postcondition; maximum 15 seconds cumulative inline sleep; approximately 2s then 4s exponential fallback with nonnegative jitter; authoritative Retry-After/reset is a lower bound and produces retry_not_before deferral when it cannot fit; at most one observe/replan cycle shares the same call, sleep, and deadline budgets. Compound ticket updates are decomposed into atomic operations and never replayed wholesale. Provisioning/readiness polling stays outside this envelope. Structured physical/logical attempt telemetry is required because historical Actions logs cannot reveal silent SDK/ACLI retries. Approval and validation are recorded in .joe-janitor/rp03-retry-envelope-validation.md and rp03-jira-failure-taxonomy.md. No tracked files or RP-04 state changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787015724450551001,"uuid":"c1e4a10f-fbba-4712-86c6-dd4796011d8f"}